okvis_port: clean-room pure-C port of OKVIS2 (work in progress)

Files under okvis_port/c/ derived from OKVIS2 (okvis_ceres/ImuError, okvis_kinematics, okvis_time, okvis_cv cameras: ok_imu, ok_time, ok_kin, ok_cam, ...) carry the
OKVIS2 BSD-3-Clause notice:
  Copyright (c) 2015, Autonomous Systems Lab / ETH Zurich
  Copyright (c) 2020, Smart Robotics Lab / Imperial College London
  Copyright (c) 2024, Smart Robotics Lab / Technical University of Munich
(full text: okvis_port/LICENSES/okvis2-BSD-3-Clause.txt). Time/Duration semantics derive from ROS time (Willow
Garage, BSD). Eigen-derived evaluation-order models (ok_eigen.c) are MPL-2.0 (Eigen 3.4.0, (c) Gael Guennebaud,
Benoit Jacob, Jitse Niesen and the Eigen authors; SelfAdjointEigenSolver/Tridiagonalization/Householder/
GeneralBlockPanelKernel/SelfadjointMatrixVector; ok_kin.c / ok_cam.c / ok_param.c / ok_err.c (module 3: manifolds, error terms, Eigen LLT and small-product models) also model Eigen's Quaternion-from-matrix
assignment, redux, 2x2 inverse and small lazy products and are therefore dual-licensed BSD-3-Clause AND MPL-2.0). BRISK files (reserved path, Codex) carry their own notices.
Module 4 (solver): ok_solve.{h,c}, ok_solve_linear.c, ok_solve_internal.h and ok_blas.{h,c} are derived from Ceres Solver
2.2.0 (Copyright 2023 Google Inc., BSD-3-Clause, full text okvis_port/LICENSES/ceres-solver-BSD-3-Clause.txt: internal/ceres
solver, program, reorder_program, parameter_block_ordering, graph_algorithms, block_jacobian_writer, program_evaluator,
residual_block, corrector, loss_function, trust_region_minimizer, trust_region_step_evaluator, dogleg_strategy,
schur_complement_solver, schur_eliminator_impl, detect_structure, dense_cholesky, invert_psd_matrix,
sparse_normal_cholesky_solver, inner_product_computer, block_sparse_matrix, eigensparse, small_blas, small_blas_generic)
and from OKVIS2 (ViGraph::optimise, ViSlamBackend::optimise{Realtime,Full}Graph); the names of Google Inc. and its
contributors may not be used to endorse derived products. ok_dense.{h,c} (dynamic-size redux, GEMV, GEBP, triangular
solvers, rank update, LLT, blocking heuristic), ok_sparse.{h,c} (SimplicialLDLT) and ok_amd.c (AMDOrdering, the
stella_port transliteration of Eigen's Amd.h) are Eigen-derived and MPL-2.0 (Eigen's LDL/AMD code is adapted upstream
from Timothy A. Davis's LDL/CSparse under a licence grant for MPL-2.0 distribution inside Eigen; no CSparse, CHOLMOD or
SuiteSparse code was read or used). The reference instrumentation (okvis_port/reference/patches/0008-solver-dump.patch,
0009-graph-twopose-problem-dump.patch) patches files of the Ceres copy inside the OKVIS2 tree and is never distributed.
Module 5 (graph): ok_twopose.{h,c} (TwoPoseGraphError, TwoPoseStandardGraphError(Const), TwoPoseExtrinsicsGraphError(Const),
PseudoInverse; the Cauchy corrector transcription inside compute() follows Ceres' corrector.cc) and ok_graph.{h,c}
(ViGraph::updateLandmarks) are OKVIS2-derived (BSD-3-Clause) and, for their Eigen 3.4.0 evaluation-order models
(small lazy products, SelfAdjointEigenSolver for n = 3 / 6 / dynamic, GEMV, fixed-size norms), MPL-2.0; ok_problem.{h,c}
(the ceres::Problem / ProblemImpl bookkeeping that defines the program order) is derived from Ceres Solver 2.2.0
(internal/ceres/problem_impl.cc, program.h, parameter_block.h, residual_block.h; BSD-3-Clause, Google Inc.).
Module 5d (graph state and mutations): ok_vigraph.{h,c} (ViGraph / ViGraphEstimator: addStates*, landmarks, observations,
priors, eliminateStateByImuMerge, freeze / unfreeze, convertToPoseGraphMst with the MstGraph Kruskal, convertToObservations,
mergeLandmark, cleanUnobservedLandmarks, two-pose const links, computeCovisibilities) are OKVIS2-derived (BSD-3-Clause,
same notices as above); the sorted-array / hash containers and the mutation-log harness are original. Patch
0010-vigraph-mutation-log.patch only instruments the OKVIS2 tree under runs/ and is never distributed.
Module 6 (ViSlamBackend): ok_vslam.{h,c} (strategy, eliminateImuFrames, applyStrategy, attemptLoopClosure,
addLoopClosureFrame, synchroniseRealtimeAndFullGraph, optimise{Realtime,Full}Graph, cleanUnobservedLandmarks, landmark merging)
and ok_vsolve.c (ViGraph::optimise on the C graph: the Ceres problem is built from the graph's Problem bookkeeping and solved
with the module-4 solver) are OKVIS2-derived (BSD-3-Clause, same notices as above; ok_vsolve.c also Ceres-derived through the
module-4 solver). ok_vsb_geom.c holds the keypoint-overlap rasterisation of ViSlamBackend::overlapFraction, which follows
OpenCV 4.6 drawing.cpp `Circle` for a filled cv::circle (Copyright (c) 2000-2022 Intel Corporation, Willow Garage, OpenCV
Foundation and the OpenCV contributors, BSD-3-Clause / Apache-2.0 since 4.5; the names of the copyright holders may not be used
to endorse derived products), and the Eigen 3.4.0 AngleAxis / Quaternion / stableNorm evaluation order (MPL-2.0); the file is
therefore dual-licensed BSD-3-Clause AND MPL-2.0. Patch 0011-backend-call-log.patch only instruments the OKVIS2 tree under
runs/ and is never distributed.
Module 7b (frontend data association): ok_frontend.{h,c} (Frontend::dataAssociationAndInitialization without place recognition:
matchToMap with its per-segment matcher, matchMotionStereo, matchStereo, removeOutliers, doWeNeedANewKeyframe, the correspondence
lists of OpenGV's FrameNoncentralAbsoluteAdapter / FrameRelativeAdapter as OKVIS2 wrote them) and ok_triangulate.c (okvis
triangulation::triangulateFast) are OKVIS2-derived (BSD-3-Clause, same notices as above) with Eigen 3.4.0 evaluation-order models
(MPL-2.0) and the OpenCV 4.6 filled cv::circle rasteriser of ok_vsb_geom.c; the files are dual-licensed BSD-3-Clause AND MPL-2.0.
Patch 0012-frontend-input-log.patch only instruments the OKVIS2 tree under runs/ and is never distributed.
Module 7c (OpenGV): ok_opengv.{h,c} (the Ransac loop, SampleConsensusProblem sampling, AbsolutePoseSacProblem / CentralRelativePoseSacProblem /
RotationOnlySacProblem as OKVIS2's Frame*SacProblem classes use them, gp3p_main glue, twopt_rotationOnly / arun, fivept_stewenius glue,
triangulate2, cayley2rot), ok_opengv_gp3p_gen.c (mechanical transcription of the OpenGV GP3P Groebner-basis solver, generated by
tools/gen_okvis_gp3p.py) and ok_opengv_stew_gen.c (OpenGV's Stewenius composeA, tools/gen_okvis_stewenius.py) are derived from OpenGV
(Copyright (c) 2013 Laurent Kneip, ANU, BSD-3-Clause, full text okvis_port/LICENSES/opengv-BSD-3-Clause.txt; the name of ANU and its
contributors may not be used to endorse derived products) and OKVIS2 (BSD-3-Clause, same notices as above), with Eigen 3.4.0 evaluation-order
models (MPL-2.0): ok_eigen_eigsolver{8,10}.c / ok_eigen_eigsolver.inc (EigenSolver<Matrix<double,N,N>>, derived from stella_port's
sv_eigen_eigensolver.c), ok_eigen_svd.c / ok_eigen_qr.c / ok_eigen_fullpivlu.c (copies of stella_port's MPL-2.0 JacobiSVD, ColPivHouseholderQR
and FullPivLU adaptations with the identifiers renamed), ok_eigen_cx.c (std::complex<double> division after the Baudin-Smith range-guarded
algorithm that libgcc >= 12 implements, multiplication, and the csqrt identity of the C library). The std::mt19937 generator and the
Lemire downscaling of libstdc++'s uniform_int_distribution are reimplemented from the standard / the documented algorithm (no libstdc++
source text). Files are dual-licensed BSD-3-Clause AND MPL-2.0 where Eigen models are involved. The reference tree links the OpenGV library
(never distributed); patch 0013-ransac-input-log.patch only instruments the OKVIS2 tree under runs/.
Module 7d (place recognition): ok_dbow.{h,c} (the DBoW2 vocabulary-tree transform, the L1 scoring database, queryL1 with the libstdc++
introsort order, Frontend::getFilteredDBoWResult) are derived from DBoW2 (Copyright (c) 2015, Dorian Galvez-Lopez, modified BSD licence, full
text okvis_port/LICENSES/dbow2-LICENSE.txt) and OKVIS2 (BSD-3-Clause). DBoW2 clause 3 ("The original author of the work must be notified of
any redistribution of source code or in binary form") is discharged: Dorian Galvez-Lopez was notified by email on 2026-10-10 of the
redistribution of ok_dbow.* in the public repository (github.com/Kraftbar/pose-validation). The BRISK
vocabulary itself (resources/small_voc.yml.gz of OKVIS2, provenance undocumented, docs/okvis2_license_audit.md) is converted at run time
by tools/convert_okvis_vocabulary.py into the gitignored runs/ tree and never copied into okvis_port. ok_place.{h,c} / ok_place_dist.c
(verifyRecognisedPlace refinement with the Ceres quickSolver reproduced through the module-4 solver, Levenberg-Marquardt strategy added to
ok_solve.c after Ceres 2.2.0 levenberg_marquardt_strategy.cc, BSD-3-Clause Google Inc.; the Eigen float evaluation-order model of the
distinctiveness statistic, MPL-2.0) and the frontend additions of ok_frontend.c are OKVIS2 / Ceres derived (BSD-3-Clause) with MPL-2.0 Eigen
models. Patch 0014-place-recognition-log.patch only instruments the OKVIS2 tree (and its DBoW2 header) under runs/.
The reference build (runs/okvis_port/reference_build) links Ceres (BSD-3 + Apache-2.0 parts), glog, gflags, OpenCV,
Boost, OpenBLAS and is never distributed. Dumps and datasets under runs/ are EuRoC-derived (non-commercial) and
must never be committed. See docs/okvis2_license_audit.md.
